--- v2.10.2/README.md
+++ v2.11.0/README.md
@@ -1,8 +1,73 @@
+# CET Native Runtime Profiler v2.11.0 — 0-Engine Scheduler attribution
+
+v2.11.0 keeps the v2.10.2 native callback profiler intact and adds a cooperative
+bridge for the PASS4/PASS4.1 `0-Engine` Scheduler.
+
+Why this exists: after callback consolidation, the native profiler can correctly
+see `0-Engine::onUpdate`, but without cooperation it cannot identify which
+scheduled child job consumed that time.
+
+With the bundled `ZERO_ENGINE_BRIDGE` Scheduler overlay installed, v2.11.0 adds:
+
+- `CET_Runtime_Profile_Scheduler_ByJob.csv`
+  - aggregate inclusive wall time per Scheduler owner/job
+  - call rate, ms/s, average and max
+- `CET_Runtime_Profile_Scheduler_Spikes.csv`
+  - chronological individual Scheduler job calls >= **2 ms** by default
+- `CET_Runtime_Profile_Scheduler_FrameBursts.csv`
+  - every job that ran in a Scheduler frame whose **combined measured job time**
+    reached **5 ms** by default
+  - this distinguishes one large child callback from several smaller jobs that
+    collided in the same frame
+
+These Scheduler CSVs are **supplemental**. Job duration is measured inside
+`0-Engine::onUpdate`, so do not add Scheduler totals to normal ByMod/Detail
+exclusive totals.
+
+The bridge registers job identity once. During capture it performs one native
+high-resolution begin/end pair per executed Scheduler job plus one begin/end
+pair per Scheduler frame. When capture is stopped, the bridge checks
+`CETProfilerIsRunning()` once per Scheduler frame and does not time individual
+jobs.
+
+Default Scheduler thresholds:
+
+```lua
+print(CETProfilerGetSchedulerJobSpikeThresholdMs())       -- 2.0
+print(CETProfilerGetSchedulerFrameBurstThresholdMs())     -- 5.0
+print(CETProfilerSetSchedulerJobSpikeThresholdMs(2.0))
+print(CETProfilerSetSchedulerFrameBurstThresholdMs(5.0))
+```
+
+For the current PASS4.1 checkpoint, keep the defaults.
+
+## Required 0-Engine bridge
+
+The native ASI alone cannot infer Lua Scheduler child identity. Install the
+bundled bridge after installing/building the profiler:
+
+```powershell
+.\Install-0Engine-ProfilerBridge.ps1
+```
+
+The installer only accepts the exact PASS4.1 v0.18.9 Scheduler baseline bundled
+for this profiler (or an already-installed bridge), and creates a backup before
+overwriting it. Restore with:
+
+```powershell
+.\Restore-0Engine-ProfilerBridge.ps1
+```
+
+The bridge is safe when the profiler ASI is absent: it detects that the v2.11
+API does not exist and runs the normal Scheduler path.
+
+---
+
